## Task 2: Interactive penguin plot

The scatterplot below compares penguin bill depth and bill length. The points are colored by species. Hover over a point to see its species, sex, island, bill depth, and bill length.

```{r}
#| label: setup
#| include: false

library(tidyverse)
library(plotly)
library(glue)
library(leaflet)
library(scales)

# Use the penguins dataset included with the assignment's specified R version.
penguins <- datasets::penguins

# Keep observations with the information needed for the plot and dashboard.
penguins_clean <- penguins |>
  drop_na(sex, species, island, bill_len, bill_dep, body_mass) |>
  mutate(
    tooltip = glue(
      "Species: {species}<br>",
      "Sex: {sex}<br>",
      "Island: {island}<br>",
      "Bill depth: {bill_dep} mm<br>",
      "Bill length: {bill_len} mm"
    )
  )
```

```{r}
penguin_plot <- ggplot(
  penguins_clean,
  aes(
    x = bill_dep,
    y = bill_len,
    color = species,
    shape = species,
    text = tooltip
  )
) +
  geom_point(size = 3, alpha = 0.85) +
  scale_color_manual(
    values = c("Adelie" = "darkorange", "Chinstrap" = "purple", "Gentoo" = "cyan4")
  ) +
  labs(
    title = "Penguin Bill Depth and Bill Length",
    x = "Bill depth (mm)",
    y = "Bill length (mm)",
    color = "Species",
    shape = "Species"
  ) +
  theme_light()

ggplotly(penguin_plot, tooltip = "text")
```

## Task 3: Interactive dashboard

The dashboard-style summary below presents the number of penguins in the cleaned dataset, the number of species, and the average body mass. It also includes an interactive map and the interactive bill measurement plot.

```{r}
penguin_count <- nrow(penguins_clean)
species_count <- n_distinct(penguins_clean$species)
average_mass <- mean(penguins_clean$body_mass, na.rm = TRUE)
```

